that the paired archive and root source bytes cannot be mixed by construction.
This does not yet bind an independently supplied typed manifest to the root or
authorize profile Import, SHA-256 inventory acceptance, or filesystem effects.

A deterministic 5,120-scalar Unicode sweep now confirms that decoded field
lookup, key copying and string-value copying produce the same UTF-8 identity
for escaped JSON source. Both copies refuse insufficient capacity without
writing bytes, including cases across BMP and supplementary Unicode planes.
This is still syntax evidence rather than a selected manifest string policy.

The portable SHA-256 domain now supports fixed-memory incremental hashing over
ordered, already admitted byte chunks, preserving partial-block state and
rejecting bit-length overflow. A read-only typed-entry chunk verifier refuses
oversized prefixes before hashing them, short streams before digest comparison,
and altered CRC-correct ZIP payloads at SHA-256 comparison. The complete file
transport and manifest-root wire binding remain open.

Fallible chunk verification now returns original upstream errors instead of
silently accepting partial input as an EOF or conflating a read failure with a
cryptographic mismatch. Both fallible and ordinary SHA-256 chunk paths share
one byte-length and digest gate; no ZIP/file source authority is introduced.

SHA-256 streaming now shares a directly testable checked byte-count helper
between hash updates and typed entry chunk verification. Synthetic values at
and above the FIPS bit-length ceiling fail safely without giant allocations.
Real profile Import must still enforce much tighter caller resource budgets.

After complete inventory and SHA-256 admission, verified ZIP members now expose
borrowed, nonzero-sized chunk iterators without allocating a second payload.
A typed member is absent only when its exact name is missing; a present empty
asset yields a valid iterator with zero chunks. All slices retain their source
provenance, and no new source or Import authority is created.

The independent `profile-entry-stream-reader` inbound adapter now hashes
already-open `Read` sources through fixed 8 KiB buffers. It preflights byte
budgets before reading and verifies exact EOF using a single extra-byte probe.
Tests distinguish short EOF, excess content, original read errors and changed
