Python `hashlib` goldens distinguish semantically equal whitespace variants;
changing another ZIP member cannot change the root-only fingerprint. This
fingerprint is not an accepted typed manifest or a declared root-hash proof.

The ordinary stored-ZIP reader now retains the complete checked source slice
as a borrow and exposes its archive-wide SHA-256 without copying. An
independent Python `hashlib` golden and changed-member regression distinguish
the whole-ZIP fingerprint from the existing root JSON fingerprint. Neither
