An independent Python `struct`/`zlib` implementation and standard `zipfile`
reader now establish byte-for-byte golden SHA-256 for the 65,534-entry ordinary
ZIP32 boundary, including empty assets, the root manifest and exact directory
count fields. It protects a 7,077,690-byte output without using ZIP64.

The same 65,534-entry golden now tests adjacent rejection boundaries:
maximum count minus one, archive bytes minus one, and aggregate payload bytes
below the final nonempty root. Writer preflight and checked ZIP reading must
return their exact resource or archive errors without treating a prefix as a
