The byte writer now supports caller-owned ZIP32 output slices with no internal
output allocation. It shares preflight, CRC and header emission with the
existing `Vec` writer; a short destination reports the exact required size
without changing a byte, and extra buffer capacity remains untouched.
The 65,534-member golden and 1,024 generated Unicode/binary archives compare
